# Recovery-mode USB gadget bring-up for leap (motorola razr 60 ultra).
#
# Pattern verified working on the 2024 arcfox (sibling Motorola foldable):
#   1. Generic recovery init.rc sets `sys.usb.configfs 0` in `on early-init`;
#      at 0 the legacy android_usb path runs, which does not exist on GKI 6.6.
#      Force configfs=1 here so the generic init.rc binds the gadget.
#   2. The dwc3 controller (a600000.dwc3 per vendor_boot bootconfig) must be
#      switched to peripheral mode before the UDC accepts a gadget binding.
#
# The mode node is reached through the /sys/class/udc symlink rather than
# /sys/bus/platform/devices/<soc>.ssusb/mode: the udc path is labelled via
# the UDC class, whereas the platform-device path needs a genfs_contexts
# entry that custom recovery sepolicy does not carry.
#
# Verified values for leap:
#   ro.hardware           = qcom          (so this filename is correct)
#   ro.boot.usbcontroller = a600000.dwc3  (from vendor_boot bootconfig)
#
# Everything else -- creating /config/usb_gadget/g1, its functions, config
# and the UDC bind -- is handled by the generic init.rc once configfs=1.

on init
    setprop sys.usb.configfs 1

on property:ro.boot.usbcontroller=*
    setprop sys.usb.controller ${ro.boot.usbcontroller}
    write /sys/class/udc/${ro.boot.usbcontroller}/device/../mode peripheral

on fs
    wait /dev/block/platform/soc/${ro.boot.bootdevice}
    symlink /dev/block/platform/soc/${ro.boot.bootdevice} /dev/block/bootdevice
